SRE Engineer Interview Questions (3–4 Years Experience)🚀 

If you're preparing for an SRE (Site Reliability Engineer) role, these are some of the most common and practical questions asked in real interviews.
They cover SLIs, SLOs, monitoring, automation, incident management, scaling, and reliability practices.

🔹 Core SRE & Reliability Concepts
• What is SRE and how is it different from DevOps?
• What are SLIs, SLOs, and Error Budgets?
• How do you calculate service availability (e.g., 99.9 vs 99.99)?
• What is toil? Share examples and how you reduced it.
• What are MTTR, MTBF, and MTTA?

🔹 Incident & Problem Management
• Explain your incident management lifecycle.
• How do you run post-incident reviews or blameless retros?
• What alerting and on-call tools have you used?
• How do you prioritize incidents during major outages?
• What’s your strategy to reduce alert fatigue?

🔹 Observability & Monitoring
• What is the difference between monitoring and observability?
• What golden signals do you always track?
• How do you design dashboards for critical services?
• What is distributed tracing and where have you used it?
• Describe a situation where logs helped you solve a major issue.

🔹 Cloud, Infrastructure & Scaling
• How do you design a highly available system?
• How does auto-scaling work in cloud environments?
• Explain the difference between L4 and L7 load balancing.
• Share your experience running Kubernetes in production.
• What steps ensure zero-downtime deployments?

🔹 Automation & CI/CD
• How do you automate recurring operational tasks?
• What is your experience with Terraform or IaC tools?
• How do you implement blue-green or canary deployments?
• What is chaos engineering and why is it useful?
• Share a scenario where automation improved reliability.

🔹 Security & Performance
• How do you handle secrets securely?
• What is latency and how do you reduce it?
• How do you identify performance bottlenecks?
• What is rate limiting and where is it used?
• What’s your experience with CDN, caching, or edge optimization?
